1 OCCU Rabbi, Rabbi of Krakow & Prague. President Council of Four Lands., Builder of the Pinchas shul in Prague. Brither-in-law of R.Moses Isserles ימ"א, Rabbi of Krak?w and Head of Council of the Four Lands, Builder of the Pinchas shul 
2 CONC in Prague
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} His signature is found on a community rule of Krakow, dated July 7, 1595
2 CONT [S.A.Zigelman - The Jews of Poland and Lithuania Until 1648].
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/KZBB-LZN/rabbi-pinchas-halevi-horowitz-of-prague%2C-parnas-of-the-4-lands-1535-1618 '''Rabbi Pinchas HaLevi Horowitz of Prague, Parnas of the 4 Lands''' ] was born in 1535, in Prague, Czechos
2 CONC lovakia, his father, Israel Jacob Munka Halevi Horowitzs (1507-1572), was then 28 years old and his mother, Nissel Reisel Ursula Stern (1507-1572), was also aged 28. He married Miryam Miriam Baila Horowitz (nee Isserles REMA's sis
2 CONC ter) in 1552, in Lesser Poland Voivodeship, Poland. They were the parents of at least 7 sons and 6 daughters. He died on 3 January, 1618.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' (13)
2 CONT Yehuda Loeb Horowitz, 1500–1630
2 CONT Rabbi Jacob ha-Levi Horowitz of Vienna, 1555–1630
2 CONT Rabbi Isaac Itzhak Yaacov Halevi Ish Horowitz, 1556–1631
2 CONT Mrs Shmuel Horowitz Reizelish, Female, 1560–1622
2 CONT Shmuel HaLevi Horowitz, 1560–1622
2 CONT David Israel HaLevi Horowitz, 1562–1625
2 CONT Hinda Halevi Katzenellenbogen Horowitz, Female. 1565–1654
2 CONT Rabbi Yehoshua "HaAruch" Rabbi of Premisla HaLevi Horowitz. 1565–1661
2 CONT Rabbi Israel Isserles HaLevi Horowitz. 1572–1623
2 CONT Sara Horowitz, Female. 1577–1657
2 CONT Rivka Horowitz, Female, 1625–1625
2 CONT Heinda Horowitz, Female,  d.1854
2 CONT Sheindel Horowitz, Femalel Deceased
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Pinchus was born in year 1535.  
2 CONT Pinchus' father was Yisrael  Yaakov HOROVITZ and his mother was Nissel Reisel Urshila.  
2 CONT His paternal grandparents were Aharon Meshulam Salman  ISH_HOROVITZ  and Esther Nechama Munk.  
2 CONT He was the oldest of ten children.  He had seven brothers and two sisters, named Jacob, Yonah, Yeshayahu, Menachem, Shmuel, Eliezer, Meshulum, Rivka  and Nechama.  
2 CONT He died, at the age of 83rd years, on March 1st, 1618.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
