2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Meir-ben-Baruch-MaHaRa-M-of-Rothenburg/6000000007987676898
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Note from https://groups.jewishgen.org/g/main/topic/rothenberg_family_tree/104356101# 15 Feb 2024 on JewishGen Groups from Dan Rottenberg, author of Finding our Fathers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yes, I'm happy to send a digital copy of my Spring 2004 Avotaynu letter setting forth my theory about descent from Rabbi Meir of Rothenburg, "The Maharam" (1215-1293).
2 CONT I've spent more than 40 years piecing together his various genealogies. As far as is know, Meir had no sons— just two daughters, whose names may have been Minna and Rebecca. One daughter married Meir's pupil Asher ben Yehiel (know
2 CONC n as "The Rosh'), who flourished isn Spain. They had eight children, but their descent is hard to trace beyond 2 or 3 generations. The other daughter was the ancestor of the Weil rabbinic dynasty of Alsace and Germany, whose branc
2 CONC hes can be traced down to the present day.
2 CONT A number of the Maharam's genealogies are accessible online. I'd be happy o hear from anyone with interest in this subject.
2 CONT Dan Rottenberg
2 CONT Philadelphia PA USA
