1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Megillat Eivah https://hebrewbooks.org/24881  which is written in Rashi script:  “....from the mouth of a great man of the holy community of Krakau, one of the princes of Israel, wise in Torah and worldly? things? 
2 CONC manhig and one of the manhigim of the lands in the kingdom of Poland. And this is the name well known? The precious mvhr”r Pinchas bn hakatsin harosh mvh” Israel [bn] Zelman Jesajahu seGal of Prag of the family of Horwitz, and his
2 CONC  (sic) [should say MY] wife, the Rabbanit marat Rechel, was daughter of marat Nachele, daughter of the sister of mvhr”r Pinchas: the honored marat Rivke Sterin who was once married in Prag to the father-in-law of my father-in-law.
2 CONC ”
2 CONT
2 CONT So here we have the source for “Rivke Stern” being the wife of Moses Ahron Teomim!  It still doesn’t explain her death year, but perhaps someone just got creative.  But what matters is that the way it is worded makes it sound like
2 CONC  our guess was right and that she was Rivke Stern in later life because of having re-married after Moses Ahron Teomim died. It is so helpful that he seems to be saying “was once married”, if I’m not reading things into it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT “Fraenkel is a rabbinic surname. It was adopted by a group of families who had sojourned in Franconia (Franken in German) during the Middle Ages, not far from the bright communities of the Rhine Valley, well known at Babylon and a
2 CONC s far as Yemen.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the ancient Jewish world, to have a rabbinic name was to be inscribed in a complex system of relationships and movements of thought...
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Teomim-Fränkels--still farther to the east: This family descends from nine children of Moses Aaron Lamël Teomim-Fränkel (XVIIth Century at Prague) and of Rivka Stern Hurwitz (daughter of Israel Horowitz, of the name of the ce
2 CONC lebrated and rich Prague family which had the favor of the Habsburgs in the XVIth Century, and lent them much).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Teomims were already known at Prague, where Rachel Teomim (equally a descendant of Horowitz) married...Yomtov Lipman Heller. In Hebrew, Teomim means 'twins.'
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Teomim-Fränkel family, which produced almost as many rabbis as the [Heller-Fränkel-Mirels] branch and occupied the totality of rabbinic posts in Eastern Europe, multiplied at Prague, in Bohemia, and swarmed [a essaimé] into G
2 CONC alicia, Podolia, and Volhynia."
2 CONT
2 CONT 1913-1996- Eger Family Association- pg. 3 - here is written born 1545 , in the Hebrew version- no date of birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wer sind die Prager Munk im 16. Jahrhundert? von Bernhard Wachstein page 146
