1 NAME Gutlin /Bachur/
2 GIVN Gutlin
2 _MARNM Bachur
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=ffb-2233
2 CONT
2 CONT Andernacht entries sometimes mention when a person’s spouse has died, or when the person is re-marrying.  Unfortunately, most of Isserl’s entries are pleas by him to be allowed to go around without wearing a “Jew badge” or to be a
2 CONC llowed to practice medicine without so many restrictions.  Poor guy.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT But the thing which gives me hope that Gutlin HO 241 was Isserl’s wife is that the Horovitz stone number for her is 2215 and his is 2214.  Since he remarried to a lady who already had a grown son (Natan Wiesbaden), it would not be
2 CONC  unusual for him to have been buried next to his first wife, the mother of his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nevertheless, it is still circumstantial.  We have to hope there is another clue out there,
