1 NAME Gutchen /Isserles/
2 GIVN Gutchen
2 SURN Isserles
2 _MARNM Grotwol
2 NICK Gutlen
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 DATE 13 NOV 1670
2 PLAC Battonnstraße Jewish cemetery, Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 NOV 1670
2 PLAC Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone Inscription: Gutchen, daughter of Mr. Schlomo Isserl. | A woman is buried here, | 3 | the pious and the expensive, | Mrs. Gitchen, daughter of the master, Mr. | Schlomo Isserles, various | 6 | and buried 
2 CONC (on) day 5, new moon Kislev | of the year 431 after a small count
2 CONT
2 CONT Commentary by Steinheim Institute:
2 CONT
2 CONT Commentary by Steinheim Institute: Dating Died, Thursday, November 13th, 1670 The religious and everyday names of daughter and father differ only slightly. Gutchen and Gitchen, or Isserl and Isserles. The name of Gutchen's husband
2 CONC  is not mentioned, although he died in 1628. Probably no tnzbh The MF indicates the day of the month with 25th Kislev. A write-off error that probably occurred during the transfer from the sk. Zl 1: The father name אסרל reflects H
2 CONC o Text faithfully. ET corrects to איסרל, which may be the correct spelling but does not correspond to the inscription. Zl 6: The new moon Kislev was celebrated 471 in two days. From the indication of the day of the week we know th
2 CONC at the 1st new moon day is meant. abbreviation not visible; Sentence separator: not recognizable
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone description Dimensions 66 x 52 x 10 cm Description Stone and writing field close with a flat arch, all-round frame, the header with the name is in the frame. State condition
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Schlomo S. Schmaja (No. ffb-0281 , Ho 482, ET 12.X.1619) Mother: Beslin (ET 27.II.1628, not with Ho) Husband: Joel Schuh Grotwol (No. ffb-0424 , Ho 532, ET 7.IX.1628) Child: Ankle to the shoe (Ho 991, ET 3
2 CONC .I.1671)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature sk P. 442, No. 32 MF, P. 48, No. 12 (ET: 58-1) ET 13.XI.1670 Dietz P. 104 (Gatte) Lö, Jewish tombstones, in: Blätter ..., III . Jg., No. 1/2, p. 14 Ho 989 HoNam p. 710: Gutchen T. Sal. Esriel HoEd: Z
2 CONC l 4: גוטכן בת כר״ר (Ho writes inaccurately here, perhaps because he is the different spelling of everyday name and religious name not considered), in the text גיטכן בת הר״ר. Zl 5 א ...., in the text אסרלס. Zl 6 יום ד׳, in the text
2 CONC  יום ה׳, as Lö noted, the new moon Kislev fell on Thursday and Friday. HoSt 824
