1 NAME Loeb /Oppenheim/ zu Worms
2 GIVN Loeb
2 SURN Oppenheim
2 NSFX zu Worms
2 _MARNM Oppenheim
2 NICK Leib
2 NICK Juda Loeb Oppenheimer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 ADDR
3 CITY Worms
3 STAE Rhineland-Palatinate
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1572 AND 1573
2 ADDR
3 CITY Worms
3 STAE RP
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It is almost completely certain that the Rivke Serle https://www.geni.com/people/Rebekka-Oppenheimer/6000000000577296894 and http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=ffb-760 who is Meir haCohen’s daughter
2 CONC  is not the one who is the widow of Loeb Oppenheim and wife or widow of Amschel Storch. There are three reasons for this. First of all, it would be odd for her sons not to be receiving money from her estate until 1583 if she had d
2 CONC ied as early as January of 1579. Second, the description of Rivke Serle on the gravestone certainly does not sound like it applies to a woman who had been married to two gaonim. Last, but most important, the name Meir is never use
2 CONC d for any of her descendants, in spite of their being so many. Josef of the weissen Loewen names a son Meir in honor of his father-in-law, but that is the only one, ever. The people who put Sorlin into Geni as the daughter of Meir
2 CONC  haCohen were just reacting to a very iffy idea by Ettlinger where he writes, surrounded by question marks, that he wonders if that grave might be Sorlin’s. But everything we have seen since then points to it being someone else.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-175298481-1-9288/juda-loeb-oppenheimer-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-110c04577f9ce61bade333555dd367a8&mrid=8711d9aec14c2e3ac7d42ab5cfa15b8d MyHeritag
