1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT A man is buried here pious and humble, who in purity and in Cleanliness entered his home It is the upright man Moshe, son of Mr. Elchanan, the memory of the righteous is a blessing He died and was buried on day 4, 5 Marcheschvan i
2 CONC n 328 after a small count.
2 CONT
2 CONT His soul is part of the bundle of life. Amen Sela
2 CONT
2 CONT Steinheim Institute Comments:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating Died Wednesday, October 8th, 1567
2 CONT
2 CONT Zl 2: cf. tSot 13.3 הי ענו הי חסיד was said about Hilel
2 CONT
2 CONT Stylistic device Rhyme on -nav in Zln 2/4, Zl 5/7 on "ar"
2 CONT
2 CONT Description Dimensions 72 x62 x14 cm
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person He married around 1545 and lived in the "red rooster".
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Hon to the red rose, then red cock Son of. Fajbes (ET 25.VIII.1550) Mother: Fogel daughter of. Majer (ET 19.IV.1550) Wife: Fradchen daughter of. Elhanan (ET 1577/78) Children: Wajbes Bacharach z.roten Hahn
2 CONC , then z. Bisemknopf (ET 19.V.1601)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature ET 8.X.1567 Dietz, p. 451 Ho 224 HoNam. P. 724: Moses S. Elchanan HoEd: Zl 1 איש, in the text אי׳. Zl 2 ה is missing. HoSt 829
