1 NAME Kalonymus Kalman /Haberksten/
2 GIVN Kalonymus Kalman
2 _MARNM Haberksten
2 NICK רבי קלונימוס בעל הנס
1 NAME R Kalonymus Kalman Haberkasten, r Ostrog, Brisk, Jerusalem Ashkenazim
1 NAME קלונימוס קלמן /הַבֶּרְקַשְׂטְן/ מהרי"ק ירושלמי, "רבי קלונימוס בעל הנ
2 GIVN קלונימוס קלמן
2 SURN הַבֶּרְקַשְׂטְן
2 NSFX מהרי"ק ירושלמי, "רבי קלונימוס בעל הנ
2 NICK רבי קלונימוס בעל הנס
1 NAME הגאון המפורסם רבי קלונימוס קלמן הַבֶּרְקַשְׂטְן, ר"מ לבוב ואוסטרהא,ראב"ד בריסק וירושלים (מכונה בשמות: מהרי"ק ירושלמי,"רבי קלונימוס בעל הנס")
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1490
2 PLAC Lvov Poland
2 ADDR
3 CITY L'viv
3 STAE L'vivs'ka oblast
3 CTRY Ukraine
1 BURI
2 DATE ABT 1550
2 PLAC Mount of Olives
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jerusalem
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1550
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jerusalem
3 CTRY Israel
1 OCCU Av Beis Din Lvov, Ostroh and Brisk, "Hayerushalmi", אב"ד בריסק
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rav Klonyimos Kalman has met with the Arizal(Rav Yitzchok Luria) and his disciple, RavChaim Vital. He is also mentioned in Sha'alos U'Teshuvos MaHarshal, Responsa 98.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Polish rabbi of the sixteenth century. He is the first known rabbi of the city of Ostrog, Volhynia, where he settled after having previously presided over a yeshibah in Lemberg. His daughter Lipka married Solomon Luria, who succee
2 CONC ded to the rabbinate of Ostrog when Haberkasten went to Palestine, about 1560. Haberkasten is known to have made the acquaintance of the great cabalists who then flourished in the Holy Land, and is mentioned by Ḥayyim Vital Calabr
2 CONC ese in the manuscript work "Liḳḳuṭe Torah."
2 CONT
2 CONT Read more: http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=15&letter=H#ixzz0pUPa8IxU
2 CONT
2 CONT Kalonymus died in Jerusalem in 1550, and was reputed to have been the holy Ari’s teacher. His greatest renown came from having saved the then-Sephardi Eliyahu Hanavi Synagogue from the bloody consequences of a blood libel. On the 
2 CONC last Saturday before Passover, neighboring Arabs dumped the body of a young boy at the synagogue and charged that Jews had baked matzos with his blood – a popular calumny that originated in 1144 in Norwich England and for spurious
2 CONC  spin-offs of which many Jews in diverse corners of the world were to pay with their lives for centuries. Somehow Kalonymus pulled off his day’s counterpart of a forensic whodunit-sensation, proved the accusers’ deceit and foiled 
2 CONC the rioters. But Kalonymus didn’t savor his victory. He berated himself for having violated the Sabbath in the course of performing his miracle. To punish himself he requested that no tombstone be erected atop his grave. He was in
2 CONC terred on the lower mountain gradient, near Rabbi Ovadia of Bertinoro (the “Bartenura”), and ordinary Jerusalemites passing by would always place stones on his unmarked grave. Over the centuries this folksy homage grew to consider
2 CONC able proportions and was visible from afar. In 1948, Arabs ripped out tombstones from the 3,000-year-old Mount of Olives Jewish cemetery and used them to construct public latrines. At that time they also savagely pulled down the g
2 CONC iant stack of stones piled up as Kalonymus’s marker during almost 400 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=10138&hilite=ec75e5d3-2c1f-4e6a-897a-e43c62c3cafa&st=%d7%90%d7%a4%d7%a8%d7%99%d7%9d+%d7%a4%d7%99%d7%a9%d7%9c&pgnum=173
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Kalonymus (Kalman) Haberkasten was a rabbi and Talmudist in sixteenth century Poland. He is well known as the rosh yeshivah of many great rabbis including Rabbi Solomon Luria, who married his daughter Lipka.
2 CONT
2 CONT Haberkasten was rosh yeshiva in Lviv (also named Lemberg: a city in western Ukraine. Capital of the historical region of Galicia; In 1349 Galicia and Lviv were incorporated into the Kingdom of Poland by King Casimir III the Great.
2 CONC  Lviv belonged to the Crown of the Kingdom of Poland 1349–1772).
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was later the first rabbi of the city of Ostroh, Volhynia (Polish: Ostróg, a historic city located in Rivne Oblast (province) of western Ukraine, located on the Horyn River), where he settled. He left Ostroh to assume the posi
2 CONC tion of rosh yeshivah in Brest  (Brisk) and Luria succeeded him in Ostroh. Haberkasten then went to Palestine, in about 1560.
2 CONT
2 CONT Haberkasten was also a Kabbalist; and he is known to have made the acquaintance of the great Kabbalists in the Holy Land, and is mentioned by Rabbi Ḥayyim Vital Calabrese in the manuscript work "Liḳḳuṭe Torah."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Alternate birthplace - L'viv Ukraine
