1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Lineage:
2 CONT
2 CONT A group of early modern manuscripts from the Jewish communities of Chełm preserves the genealogical chain linking Rabbi Eliyahu Baal Shem to the later Kelma and Fraenkel families. The Pinkas Kehillat Chełm (NLI Heb. Ms. 8° 412) id
2 CONC entifies Rabbi Eliyahu Baal Shem explicitly as “Eliyahu son of Aharon Yehuda of Chełm,” establishing the foundational generation. The Sefer HaYuchasin of Chełm (NLI Heb. Ms. 4° 1782) continues this line with his son, Rabbi Aharon 
2 CONC Yehuda Kelma, while the fragmentary Megillat Chełm (NLI F 12345) records the next generation, Rabbi Eliyahu Aharon Kelma, and even mentions a descendant named Uri Lipman, corresponding to Rabbi Uri Lipman Fraenkel. A marginal glos
2 CONC s in a manuscript of the Maharshal’s Responsa (NLI Heb. Ms. 8° 623) further confirms that the Eliyahu of Chełm mentioned in the responsum is indeed “Eliyahu Baal Shem.” Taken together, these manuscripts form a coherent documentary
2 CONC  chain supporting the lineage: Baal Shem → Aharon Yehuda → Eliyahu Aharon Kelma → Uri Lipman Fraenkel.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From: '''http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=30378&st=&pgnum=17'''
2 CONT
2 CONT English translation:
2 CONT ''From the genealogy of [https://www.geni.com/people/Meshulam-Zalman-Auerbach/6000000004957016884 Rabbi Meshulam Zalman Auerbach]: We know that he had four adult sons and a daughter, who was married to the eminent rabbi Ori Lipman
2 CONC  Darshan, son of Rabbi Aaron, who served as a rabbi in several communities in Israel, and later was appointed as a judge and director of rabbinical affairs in the imperial city of Vienna when the rabbi ([http://www.geni.com/people
2 CONC /R-Gershon-Oulif-Ashkenazi/6000000007672065934 Gershon Oulif Ashkenazi]), author of the work "Avodat HaNeresh" was the head rabbi there. In 1669, he approved the book [https://cja.huji.ac.il/gross/browser.php?mode=set&id=38153  "O
2 CONC r Hadash" written by Rabbi Chaim Buchner] (who passed away in 1671), and it is inscribed with these words: "The great preacher, who previously taught Torah in Israel. He was a rabbi and head rabbi in several holy communities, know
2 CONC n as Rabbi Lipman Darshan of Vienna."''
2 CONT
2 CONT Français:
2 CONT
2 CONT "De la généalogie du rabbin Meshulam Zalman Auerbach : Nous savons qu'il avait quatre fils adultes et une fille, mariée au rabbin éminent Ori Lipman Darshan, fils du rabbin Aaron, qui a servi comme rabbin dans plusieurs communauté
2 CONC s en Israël, puis a été nommé juge et directeur des affaires rabbiniques dans la ville impériale de Vienne lorsque le rabbin, auteur de l'ouvrage "Avodat HaNeresh" y était grand rabbin. En 1669, il a approuvé le livre "Or Hadash" 
2 CONC écrit par le rabbin Chaim Buchner (décédé en 1671), et il est inscrit ces mots : "Le grand prédicateur, et auparavant il enseignait la Torah en Israël. Il a été rabbin et grand rabbin dans plusieurs communautés saintes, connu sous
2 CONC  le nom Rabbi Lipman Darshan de Vienne.""
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Veisberg: Hebrew printers in Sulzbach (CF Charles p. Stanton Family Collection 1802-2001 - Page 298 -  http://www.archive.org/stream/charlesperrystanton_04_reel04#page/n325/mode/1up ).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Uri Lipmann, father of [http://www.geni.com/people/Aaron-ben-Uri-Lipmann-Fraenkel/6000000006911140325 Ahron (ben Uri Lipmann Fraenkel)], was | a son-in-law of [http://www.geni.com/people/Meshulam-Zalman-Auerbach/60000000049570168
2 CONC 84 Auerbach] | a member of the lasr Vienna rabbinate under the presidency of Gerson Ulif. He was a celebrated speaker ... " His house, [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herrengasse 90 herrengasse], was one of the best in the Getto. Ne
2 CONC wly built it reflected the wealth and taste of the owner. The stone steps, the ornaments in front, a lovely garden with its own cottage, these gave an impression of elegance" according to Kauffman ( Die letzte Verteibung). One of 
2 CONC his daughters ([http://www.geni.com/people/Resel-RIES/6000000013632034567 Resel]l) was married to [http://www.geni.com/people/Yaakov-Koppel-Model-Ries/6000000000348866589 Koppel Ries], a son of his colleague, Model Levi Oettingen.
2 CONC  Koppel Ries, thus brother-in-law of Ahron (ben Uri Lipmann Fraenkel), later was a respected member of the Viennese exiles in Berlin. Uri Lipmann had occupied several rabbinates before his Vienna appointement..."
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT In Vienna:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=76&letter=V#230
2 CONT
2 CONT "The last rabbi of Vienna and of Lower Austria was [http://www.geni.com/people/R-Gershon-Oulif-Ashkenazi/6000000007672065934 Gershon Ashkenazi](C1625-1693)., whose colleagues were Mordecai Löb Oettingen (the friend of the Christia
2 CONC n divine Wagenseil) and the preachers '''Uri Lipmann'''[ , ] Hirz Koma and Enoch Fränkel."
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Also named:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1/ Uri LIEPMANN
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: page 212 of  [http://www.archive.org/stream/dieletztevertre00kaufgoog#page/n200/mode/2up  "Die letzte Vertreibung der Juden aus Wien und Niederösterreich: Ihre Vorgeschichte (1625-1670) und Ihre Opfer" David Kaufmann -Budapes
2 CONC t, 1889]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2/"Hagaon hagadol" Uri LIPPMAN
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: Page: vol. 1, p. 11 of: Genealogical tables of Jewish families: 14th-20th centuries: forgotten fragments of the history of the Frænkel family. Louis Frænkel, Henry Frænkel, Georg Simon K.G.Saur, München (Munich), 1999
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1667 [http://www.geni.com/people/Guetel-Fraenkel/6000000013632143318 Gitel] married the printer Aron in Sulzbach, who was a son of Hagaon hagadol Uri Lippman from Vienna."
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Grabschriften des Alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien by Dr. Bernhard Wachstein- Band I-page 438 &  page 540 nachtrag 60.
