1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE: There are two Menachem Mendel Auerbachs: 1) https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Menachem-Mendel-Auerbach-author-of-Ateret-Zekenim/6000000004210360913: Otser HaRabanim # 13391 son of Meshulam Zalman Fischof # 15
2 CONC 747, and 2) https://www.geni.com/people/R-Menachem-Mendel-Auerbach-the-Younger-A-B-D-Krotoschin/6000000002802422237: Otser HaRabanim # 13392, son of Moshe Auerbach # 14391. They were both rabbis at Krotoschin at one time or anothe
2 CONC r. Based on the Wunder source, only Menachem #1 (the elder) was the s-i-l of https://www.geni.com/people/Yosef-Katz-HaCohen/6000000136694716822. Therefore, the two women, Rebecca Rivke and Esther, who were both previously shown as
2 CONC  daughters of https://www.geni.com/people/Yosef-Katz-HaCohen/6000000136694716822 and married to Menachem Mendel Auerbach #1 and # 2, are most likely the same person, married only to Menachem Mendel Auerbach #1. This mistake has be
2 CONC en corrected by detaching the one shown to be married to Menachem Mendel #2 and merging them as the wife of Menachem Mendel #1. I do not know which of the given names is more correct. (24 NOV 2024)
2 CONT
2 CONT Name is possibly Esther. 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: There is no indication in any source of there being two daughters of https://www.geni.com/people/Yosef-Katz-HaCohen/6000000136694716822 having married https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Menachem-Mendel-Auerbach-author-of-Ater
2 CONC et-Zekenim/6000000004210360913, but perhaps this is what is behind the two different given names previously appearing as married to Menachem Mendel grandfather and Menachem Mendel grandson. Future researchers should remain open to
2 CONC  the possibility of there having been two spouses who were sisters. (25 NOV 2024) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca's father, Yosef Yehuda Lieb Katz, was the father-in-law of Menachem Mendel Auerbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Elef Margaliot by Rabbi Meir Wunder, Page 493, Entry 711 (1993)
