1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Die Familie Teomim", by Leopold Lowenstein:  "Moshe Aron Lamel Teomim  Frankel in Prague, nicknamed Aron Munk, who died around the middle of the 16th century; his wife Rifka Stern was the daughter of Israel Horwit
2 CONC z, who died in Prague in 1572, and the sister of R. Pinchas Horwitz, brother-in-law of R. Moses Isserles, 4 sons and 5 daughter from this marriage."
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Jacobi Papers":  "R. Moshe Aharon Laemmel-Munk-Teomim... d. in Cracow before 1609.  Early he moved to Prague where in 1573 he succeeded to the Kehilla and other privileges (including those in the Pinkas-Shul) of his father-in
2 CONC -law, adopting also the latter's vernacular surname "Munk"; in 1578 he acquiesed in the new Kehilla Regulations prepared by the imperially appointed MaHaRaM miPadua ... and two further rabbinical authorities, providing, inter alia
2 CONC , that nobody should serve as rabbi or lay leader for the Prague Kehilla unless duly elected by the Kehilla according to those regulations.  He became the 'Stammvater einer unuebeschbaren Zahl von Gelehrten'..." [ancestor of an in
2 CONC numerable number of scholars]
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the son of Nathan Veidel. http://sammlungen.ub.uni-frankfurt.de/freimann/content/pageview/664362
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT birth year disputed - 1560, 1550, 1585, 1521???
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.nameplanets.com/Family_Tree/default.htm date listed as c1550 - 1608 (Feldblum Yolles Family Tree)
2 CONT
