2 CONT A transcript of Ogla’s tombstone inscription can be seen [http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=46800&st=&pgnum=43&hilite here].
2 CONT
2 CONT Ogla was a nickname for Avigail ([https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/1664214/jewish/What-D Source]).
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Ogla's parents are unknown. She has often been confused with https://www.geni.com/people/Olka/6000000066151278031. See [https://www.geni.com/discussions/163420 this discussion]. Edward Gelles ([http://archives.balliol.ox.a
2 CONC c.uk/Modern%20Papers/gelles/Some%20Family%20Connections%20with%20Wahl%20-%20Katzenellenbogen.pdf here]) does claim that Abigail Ogla was a Jaffe. However he provides no source for this. Whilst he doesn't go so far as to say she wa
2 CONC s a daughter of Rabbi Mordechai Jaffe - Levush, only a relative, it does seem to be a mistake.
