1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wer sind die Prager Munk im 16. Jahrhundert? von Bernhard Wachstein   page 146
2 CONT
2 CONT https://zayt.org/collections/pragapublica/2169?p=47
2 CONT https://zayt.org/collections/pragapublica/2169?p=52
2 CONT https://zayt.org/collections/pragapublica/2169?p=125
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on the provided documents and our previous conversation, here is what we know about Rabbi Kywa (written as "Kywa rabi" in the historical text):
2 CONT He was a property owner in late 16th-century Prague: As we discussed earlier, he is the central figure in a 1577 real estate contract recorded in the Liber Judeorum Albus (The White Book of the Jews)
2 CONT . In this transaction, he purchased a house in the Jewish quarter for 150 Bohemian groschen from Salomon Kurc and Salomon Landa
2 CONT . The property was situated between the houses of Israel Munk and Josef Juda
2 CONT .
2 CONT His family connections: Another document from the same registry, dated 1581, introduces us to his family. It mentions his wife, Sara ("Sara Kywy rabi zida ziena"), who was involved in her own property transfer
2 CONT . Through this record, we also learn that Rabbi Kywa's brother-in-law was Rabbi Pinkas ("rabi Pinkas bratr gegij" - Rabbi Pinkas, her brother)
2 CONT .
