1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moses_ben_Isaac_Bonems '''Moshe HaCohen Meisels'''] was a great-grandson of Moses Isserles, and later became the son-in-law of Samuel Eliezer Edels. He was successively rabbi at Liubo
2 CONC ml (Volhynia) and Lublin. In the approbations to works given by the members of the Council of Four Lands at the Gramnitza (candlestick) fair on 6 April 1664, Moses signed first. He was the author of novellæ on the Talmud, publishe
2 CONC d with the Ḥiddushe Halakot, last recension (Mahdura Batra), of R. Samuel Edels (Lublin, 1670). He died in Lublin on 25 November 1668.
