1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sources:
2 CONT *[http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=10126&st=&pgnum=2 '''Meir Ashkenazi in Hebrew Books''']
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://hebrewbooks.org/9422  Hebrew Books ספר ״גבורות אנשים״ ב]
2 CONT
2 CONT Pupil of Jesue Falk (Sema) and of Maharam Lublin.  Instructed his famous son in his early Talmudic learning (iv 5).
2 CONT
2 CONT R' Meir Hakohen Askenazi of Bohemia was born in 1579 and died in 1643.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of R' Moshe Hakohen Ashkenazi.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Adam Cherson added:'''''
2 CONT As shown by the media files from the book Ele Toldot [Burial records of the Jewish community of Frankfurt am Main], 1241-1824] posted on the pages of https://www.geni.com/people/Golda-Bingen-Katz/6000000011187168435 and https://ww
2 CONC w.geni.com/people/Meir-Bingen-zur-Leiter/6000000000157515085, the spouse of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Meir-Hakohen-Katz-Ashkenazi/60000... was a Golde bat Meir ben Moshe of Bingen. Golde was not the daughter of Ziskind of 
2 CONC Bingen, who these documents show was her brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Meir was the husband of the daughter of Itzhak Katz of Posneh. In amistava he had two sons - Shabty (the ShaCh)  and Yona Menachem Nachum, and one (or 2?) daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Cherson added: 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Av Beth-Din (Head of the Jewish Court) in Vilna.
