1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT il épouse Gutlen Isserles, fille de Shlomo Isserles
2 CONT
2 CONT sa tombe à Francfort est voisine de celle de Gitchen Metz, épouse de Gumpricht Metz (Faustini p. 69)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Tombstone Inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joel Schuh Grotwol. | A man is buried here, upright | 3 | and faithful, Mr. Joel, | Son of Shlomo, his memory for a blessing, various | and buried (on) day 5, 9. | 6 | Elul 388 after a small count. | His soul is bound in the bundl
2 CONC e of life in the Garden of Eden, Amen
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments by Steinheim Institute:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Comments by Steinheim Institute:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating died Thursday, 07.09.1628 Ho reads beiה ​​instead of שפ״ח for the year and thus calculates 1625. The sk confirms 1628. In the sk the name יואל שוא is given , ET corrects שור to שוך, which in turn corresponds to "shoe". The 
2 CONC house "Schuh" was built in 1560 "from a stable belonging to the Haas between Reuss and Garlic for Joel and Michael called Gerotwohl, Sons of the Schlom zum Haas" (Dietz, p. 472). Grotwohl seems to be an old family name of this wid
2 CONC ely ramified family. (Dietz, p. 136) Zl 2: טמן instead of טמון for rhyme reasons. Abbreviation points sentence separator: diamonds
2 CONT
2 CONT Stylistic device Rhyme with -man in lines 2 and 3 Top of the page description Dimensions 75 x70 x17 cm Description almost square stele with a slightly curved end, recessed inscription field, a header. Condition The last line is we
2 CONC athered.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person He lived in the Schuh house and married in 1605.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Schlomo ben Jizchak Schuh (No. ffb-0444 , Ho 410, ET 21.V.1607) Mother: Edel bat. Josef Oppenheim (No. ffb-0421 , Ho 792, ET 2.XI.1654) Wife: Gutchen bat Schlome Isserles ( ffb-0420 , Ho 989, ET 13.XI.1670
2 CONC ) Child: Amschel zum Schuh (Ho 991, ET 3.I.1671)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature sk, p. 56, No. 92 MF: - ET 7.IX.1628 Dietz, p. 135f. (Family), p. 472 (house) Ho 532 HoNam p. 709: Grotwol Joël HoEd: Zl 5 י״ט, in the text ט׳. Zl 6 שפ״ה, in the text שפ״ח. HoSt 821
