1 NOTE {geni:about_me} n February 1712, [https://www.geni.com/people/Elhanan-Fraenkel/6000000042444061795 Elkan and Zwi Hirsch Fränkel] (on Geni) were arrested following a denunciation by a convert, Ischay Fränkel. Elkan was accused of p
2 CONC ossessing blasphemous books, influencing the court politically, and embezzling public funds. Zwi Hirsch was alleged to have written a book on witchcraft. A personal enemy headed the investigating commission. Elkan was taken into c
2 CONC ustody and placed in solitary confinement. Despite a lack of evidence, the accusations were declared true. The Margrave did not protect him but instead sentenced him to flogging, life imprisonment, confiscation of his property, an
2 CONC d the expulsion of his family. Rabbi Zwi Hirsch also remained imprisoned until 1723 and died around 1739 in Georgensgmünd, where a Jewish community with a synagogue existed.
