2 CONT Rabbi Jacob of Worms. He was the great Rabbi, Rosh and AB"D for the whole area of Aschkenas, and he too was gathered to his people in that year. He, Rabbi J. z"l, was the uncle: the brother of the father of the four   gaon brother
2 CONC s, Roshei Yeshiva: mh"rr Chaim [Rabbi of] Friedberg; mhr"r Liwa [Maharal]; mh"rr Sinai; and mh"rr Shimshon. All of them epitomes of their generation and ?? from whom light shone forth??
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Memoiren des Ascher Levi. Footnote is mistaken, as David Gans writes in Zemach David that Rabbi Jacob from Worms was the paternal uncle, brother of the father of the Maharal. The descendant names make sense that way also.
