1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Rabbi Betzalel "Charif" LOEW (1547 - 1599 d. Kolin) was the firstborn (perhaps not) son of the Maharal of Prague, Rabbi Judah LOEW. His descendants include 7 generations of Rabbis.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Rabbi Shmuel LOEW (b. 14 Jan. 1576, d. 1655) married Rosa
2 CONT
2 CONT           o daughter LOEW m. her relative R. Haim CATZ from Posnan (descendant of         MAHARAL)
2 CONT
2 CONT           o daughter LOEW m. Jacob the son of Rabbi Haim from Hessen
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Rabbi Yehuda Leib LOEW (b. 1611, d. 1704)
2 CONT
2 CONT                 + Rabbi Moshe LOEW of Posen (b. 1663, d. around 1736 Minsk)
2 CONT
2 CONT                       # Rabbi Schneur ZALMAN LOEW (b. 1692, d. ~1735)
2 CONT
2 CONT                             * Rabbi Boruch Hatzadik LOEW (b. ~1721, d. ~1790) m. Rivkah
2 CONT
2 CONT                                   o [2] Yehuda Leib LOEW
2 CONT
2 CONT                                         + [4] Yishai. Son: Neched Hashearit Yehuda Zeev WOLF (d. 21 Aug. 1882 Jerusalem). 
2 CONT
2 CONT                                   o Mordechai POISNER (d. 23 Feb. 1823 Kapost)
2 CONT
2 CONT                                   o Moshe (b. Leozna)
2 CONT
2 CONT                                   o Sarah m. Israel KOZAK
2 CONT
2 CONT                                   o Akiva FRIDKIN m. the sister of the wife of Rabbi SEGAL the elder, daughter of Yehuda Leib SEGAL and Bila.
2 CONT
2 CONT                                   o [3] Rabbi Schneur ZALMAN BORUCHOVITCH of Liadi (Laydie) (The Alter Rebbe founder of Chabad) (b. 15 Sep. 1745, d. 1812 or 1813). Chabad has a publication enumerating his descendants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Rabbi Mendel Mark LOEW (died young) m. Gitel Kitel Sara
2 CONT
2 CONT     * R. Kaufman Yekutiel LOEW m. Gitl Elisabeth (d. 1618 Prague)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Lift LOEW (d. 1613 Prague) m. Rabbi Pinhas HOROWITZ (d. 3.11.1653 Prague). They had no children. Rabbi Pinhas remarried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The Maharal's marriage to his wife Pearl was a very happy one, and they were blessed with seven children, six daughters and a son. All six daughters married into prominent Prague families. His son, Bezalel, became rabbi in Cologne
2 CONC , Germany, where he headed a rabbinical academy. The Maharal was deeply grieved when this son met an untimely death in 1600. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
