2 CONT From the JewishEncyclopedia.com (1906):
2 CONT
2 CONT HEILBRONN (HEILPRIN), ABRAHAM BEN MOSES ASHKENAZI:
2 CONT
2 CONT By: Richard Gottheil, M. Seligsohn
2 CONT
2 CONT Chief rabbi of Lemberg; born in 1578; died Jan. 2, 1649.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was related to R. Solomon Edels.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Heilbronn wrote: "Birkat Abraham," a homily which he delivered on the day of his "bar miẓwah" (Prague); "Ahabat Ẓiyyon," a commentary on the Pentateuch and the five Megillot (Lublin, 1639). In the preface to the latter wor
2 CONC k he asserts that he also wrote a commentary on the Prophets and the Hagiographa, and he refers to a work of his entitled "Sha'are Ẓiyyon."
2 CONT
2 CONT     ******************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Represented Ruthenia region at Council of Four Lands: 1627-28: Table 6(h), p. 156: https://muse.jhu.edu/article/846614
