2 CONT
2 CONT R. Abraham (Joseph Jacob) Ashkenazi-(Katzenellenpogen) born about 1549.
2 CONT
2 CONT Became Rabbi of Janow about 1593.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1615, was elected ABD of Lvov.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in Lvov April 30 (6 Iyar) 1637
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Avraham (Joseph Jacob) Katzenellenbogen was a Polish rabbi; born in 1549. He died at Lemberg, April 30, 1637.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the grandfather of Ezekiel Katzenellenbogen, author of "Keneset Yehezkel". Together with his brother Mattithiah Libermann he studied under his uncle Isaac Katzenellenbogen, rabbi  of Neustadt, and autho of "Moledot Yizhak".
2 CONT
2 CONT At first rabbi of Yanow, near Lemberg (c 1593) he was elected in 1615 at Lemberg to succeed Moses Harif, who, recognising Katzenellenbogen's scholarship, voluntarily resigned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Katzenellenbogen remained in Lemberg until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the novellae are quoted in  "Birkat Tob" by R. Moses of Metz, and he is mentioned in the responsa of Meir of Lublin and in the "Etan ha-Ezrahi" of Avraham ben Israel Jehiel Rapoport.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT *Michael, Or ha-Hayyim, no 118
2 CONT *Nepi-Ghirondi, Toledot Gedole Yisrael, pp 6
2 CONT *Buber, Anshe Shem, pp 2-4, Cracow, 1895
2 CONT *Eisenstadt-Wiener, Da'at Kedoshim, pp 87, 92,93
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (1990)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT né vers 1570? 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Polish rabbi; born in 1549; died at Lemberg April 30, 1637; grandfather of Ezekiel Katzenellenbogen, author of "Keneset Yeḥezḳel." Together with his brother Mattithiah Liebermann he studied under his uncle Isaac Katzenellenbogen, 
2 CONC rabbi of Neustadt, and author of "Moledot Yiẓḥaḳ." At first rabbi of Yanow, near Lemberg (c. 1593), he was elected in 1615 at Lemberg, to succeed Moses Ḥarif, who, recognizing Katzenellenbogen's scholarship, voluntarily resigned. 
2 CONC Katzenellenbogen remained in Lemberg till his death. Some of his novellæ are quoted in "Birkat Ṭob" by R. Moses of Metz, and he is mentioned in the responsa of Meïr of Lublin and in the "Etan ha-Ezraḥi" of Israel Jehiel Rapoport.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Abraham (Joseph Jacob) ben Joel Katzenellenbogen: Polish rabbi; born in 1549; died at Lemberg April 30, 1637; grandfather of Ezekiel Katzenellenbogen, author of "Keneset Yeḥezḳel." Together with his brother Mattithiah Liebermann h
2 CONC e studied under his uncle Isaac Katzenellenbogen, rabbi of Neustadt, and author of "Moledot Yiẓḥaḳ." At first rabbi of Yanow, near Lemberg (c. 1593), he was elected in 1615 at Lemberg, to succeed Moses Ḥarif, who, recognizing Katz
2 CONC enellenbogen's scholarship, voluntarily resigned. Katzenellenbogen remained in Lemberg till his death. Some of his novellæ are quoted in "Birkat Ṭob" by R. Moses of Metz, and he is mentioned in the responsa of Meïr of Lublin and i
2 CONC n the "Etan ha-Ezraḥi" of Israel Jehiel Rapoport.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography: Michael, Or ha-Ḥayyim, No. 118; Nepi-Ghirondi, Toledot Gedole Yisrael, p. 6; Buber, Anshe Shem, pp. 2-4, Cracow, 1895; Eisenstadt-Wiener, Da'at Ḳedoshim, pp. 87, 92, 93.
2 CONT
2 CONT מגלות היוחסין של משפחות יהודיות הונגריות- כרך ראשון עורך- מונקאטשי pg. 152
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Inschriften des alten Judenfriedhofe in Wien" Dr. Bernard Wachstein, Band I -  page 294
