2 CONT
2 CONT According to Prof Hava Turniansky, Chajes comes from Chaja's חיה׳ס, like Sirkes, Etkes, etc. Hence Chajes is the spelling in la'az not Chajos or Chajus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Michael Rony:  Most family members lived in Eastern Galicia, around Lemberg/Lvov/Lviv. In the Polish records where they were called Chajes. In the Hebrew sources they spell their name as חיות. A few of these migrated to Hungar
2 CONC y and are listed in the Hungarian records as Chajes. The Hebrew spelling raises doubts about the derivation of the name from the name Chaje, unless you accept the theory that the family preferred to be known as the "animals" inste
2 CONC ad of the descendants of a woman by the name of Chaje. More likely the name means something like vitality and the modern Hebrew pronunciation of Chayut reflects the original meaning better than the Yiddish pronunciation.
2 CONT
