2 NOTE The genius Rabbi Shabbtai HaKohen was a judge in the holy congregation of Vilna, and afterwards was Chief of the Rabbinical Court in Holesov which is in the country of Moravia, and there is his resting place, in the year 5421 (166
3 CONC 1), at 41 years old. Author the the book "Shiftei Kohen" (a commentary) on Shulchan Aruch and other books known (by the name of his magnum opus) as the Shach. (He was the) brother of the wondrous genius Rabbi Yonah Nachum Katz Chi
3 CONC ef of the Rabbinical Court of Sochaczew, in the region of Warsaw. They were the sons of the greatest genius in his generation, our master Rabbi Meir HaKohen who was Chief of the Rabbinical Court of Amstibov and (its surrounding) a
3 CONC rea, and afterwards Chief of the Rabbinical Court of Mogilev, and his resting place is in the city of Dubna (he died) in the year 5403 (1643). He was the son of the great genius, our master, Rabbi Moshe HaKohen Chief of the Rabbin
3 CONC ical Court of Thannhausen near the city of Ansbach, and increasing in holiness, his lineage (implicitly his direct paternal line) ascends until Eli the Kohen (technically Kohen Gadol, or High Priest) peace be upon him, may his mer
3 CONC it protect us.
