2 NOTE Translation of the Hungarian and Hebrew text in this document: "Let everyone who sees this document know that Ábrahám Bumizil declared to me that András, a non-Jew, had forgiven his debt of twenty forints, which was due at Christm
3 CONC as, until Carnival. However, he has no right to demand anything from him until Carnival, even without interest. Akiba b. Menachem HaCohen." and then: "The signature of the document is the first written trace and data found in Hung
3 CONC ary about the scholar Akiba Kohen Nási, who according to old foreign Jewish literature in Hungary before 1496 he was in a prestigious official position among our ancestors and then emigrated to Prague - for reasons still unknown. 
3 CONC B.M."
