2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT According to his own biography and the biographical notes by his son Samuel, he was born in the year 1577 several days after the death of his father Nathan or Nassen. He was raised by his grandfather: Moses Wallerstein Levi Heller
2 CONC  in Vienna.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 13 (about 1599/80) he was sent to study in Prague with the MaHaRaL at the MaHaRaL's yeshiva.
2 CONT
2 CONT Next he studied Torah with Rav Jacob Ginsburg in Friedland.
2 CONT
2 CONT At 18 (about 1595) he was appointed a member of the MaHaRaL's judicial court in Prague, a position he held for 27 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1622, he left Prague for Nicholsburg where he served as Rabbi and Chief of the Bet Din. However, after 6 months he was called to serve in Vienna, the capital city of Austria as chief of the Bet Din. The post was considered of m
2 CONC ajor importance in the world wide Jewish community as Vienna at that time was one of the largest existing Jewish communities.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1627, he was chosen Bet Din of Prague. However, after only 6 months, on 4 Jul 1629, he was imprisoned for 40 days after which he was released penniless. He was forbidden to practice his profession as well.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1630 the ban was lifted and in 1631, he was asked to take a position in Nimerov.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1634 he was elected rabbi in Ludmir where he remained for a total of 7 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1641 he became Chief Bet Din and Rav of the Jewish community in Krakow where he died the 6 Elul in 1654. He is buried in the Krakow cemetery along the fence in the area devoted to the poor and the needy.
2 CONT
