1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone Inscription: Sorlin Bonn. | Here | 3 | is a woman buried, well regarded and worthy | Mrs. Sorlin, daughter of the chief | 6 | and daughter of the Aharon Bonn, | different eve of holy Shabbat and buried | 
2 CONC on day 1, 13. Kislev 416 | 9 | after a small count. Your soul is involved in the bundle of life with the other just men and women in the Garden of Eden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Steinheim Institute Commentary: Dating Died, Friday, December 10th, 1655 Sorle named Bonn with the name of her father. The name of a spouse is not mentioned. The reason may be that she was married three times. All three spouses di
2 CONC ed before her. Sorlen (HoSt. 991) was buried near her first husband Feibesch (HoSt.989) and next to Süsmann Mainz (ET 16.VIII.1600, Ho 367, HoSt. 992). Abbreviation squiggle, "flowers" and a tilde; Sentence separator:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone description Dimensions 95 x 65 x 15 cm Description Stele with all-round frame and flat arch finish. Flowers as an ornament. Condition Zln 7/8 partly damaged or weathered.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person From the first and third marriage, ET names three children each. Sorlen was married three times. She lived in the bisem button, then in the white horse and finally in the green door.
2 CONT
2 CONT About the family Father: Aharon Bonn (No. ffb-0057 , Ho 5563 / undated , ET around 1623) Mother: Lea Gutlen (No. ffb-3388 ^ & 3405A + B, Ho 420, ET 27.II.1609) Husband I: Feibesch Bacharach (No. ffb-0469 , Ho 373, ET 19.V.1601) Hu
2 CONC sband II: Gumpel KaZ, from whom probably divorced (Ho 674, ET 27.IV.1636) Husband III: Herz KaZ, died in 1645 (not at Ho, ET 22.III.1645) Brother: Nathan Bonn (No. ffb-0629 , Ho 171 with wrong date, ET 25.XI.1629)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature sk, p. 312, no. 76 MF, p. 34, no. 1 (ET: 39-3) ET 10.XII.1655 Dietz Ho 804 HoNam p. 700: Bonn Sorle HoEd: Zl 7 ?????? , in the text ??????. Zl 8 ????, in the text ?????. Zl 9 ????, in the text ?????.
2 CONC  HoSt 991
