1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Meisels/6000000188025362831 and of https://www.geni.com/people/Esther-Ashkenazy/6000000003925332590, whose name is probably not Esther (name unknown). (30 AUG 2024) 
2 CONT
2 CONT      ****************************
2 CONT
2 CONT \The name esther is uncertain, as is the following, which has several versionsof who was involved. However, the story is that during the 1648 Chmelnietski massacres, the father was killed and esther was separated from her brother,
2 CONC  Shabtai/Shabsai. years later, she heard what she thought was her father's learning style and went over to the person doing the exposition. She found her long-lost brother who had learned at his father's knee in that style. the br
2 CONC other was Rav Shabtai Cohen, author of the Siftei Cohen, the Schach!
2 CONT
2 CONT it is know that the Maharam A"sch was a grand nephew of the Schach from a "haskama" of the Schach's other brother, Rav Yona Nachum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eli Handel: Dr. David Dubin wrote to me as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT There was uncertainty whether the Maharam was the Shach's nephew or grandnephew. Then a relatrive found a Haskama written by a brother of the Shach mentioning his sister's grandson Rav Meir. Thus, the Maharam was son of Rav Yitzch
2 CONC ak. Rav Yitzchak was the son-in-law of Esther, the Shach's sister, daughter of Rav Meir son of Rav Moshe.
