1 NAME Salomon Isaac /Grotwol/
2 GIVN Salomon Isaac
2 _MARNM Grotwol
2 NICK Schlomo Schuh Grotwohl
2 NICK Zalman Grotwohl z. Schuh S. Jitschak
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 MAY 1607
2 PLAC Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 22 MAY 1607
2 PLAC Battonnstraße Jewish cemetery, Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Salomon Shlomo Isaac Grotwol zum Schuh, cité de 1592 à 1606 dans sa maison zum Schuh (Faustini p. 69)
2 CONT
2 CONT né en 1537 selon certains, entre 1535 et 1540
2 CONT
2 CONT il épouse Edel Oppenheim, fille de Joseph Oppenheim
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Tombstone Inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT The benefactor Schlomo Schuh Grotwol.	 In .... Ben Schemen?	 the Schlomo vineyard in Baal-	 Hammon, it's kept there, hidden	 and safe, keeper of truth	 and loyalty to his soul (good) he shows	 a man ... in (with) his body,	 ... in
2 CONC  (with) his fortune, Schlomo,	 ... ol?, different at night	 2 and bury day 3, 25th Ijar	 367. His soul is part of the bundle of life	
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes of Steinheim Institute:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dating Died, Monday, May 21, 1607 Zl 1: alef-lamed ligature. Zl 2: Isa 5.1. Zl 3 / 4a: Hld 8.11. Zl 5b / 6a: Composed of Ps 146, and Isa 25.2. Zl 6b: Prov 11.17. Zl 9: alef-lamed ligature. Abbreviation points; Sentence separator: 
2 CONC double rhombuses?
2 CONT
2 CONT Stylistic device Rhyme up
2 CONT
2 CONT Headstone description Dimensions 130 x 110 x 18 cm house sign shoe condition weathering in Zln 2/3 and 7-9
2 CONT
2 CONT About the person Schlomo was a cloth dealer
2 CONT
2 CONT About  the family Father: Jizchak Mother: unknown Wife: Edel T. Josef Oppenheim (No. ffb-0421 , Ho 792, ET 2.XI.1654) Children: Liwa (No. ffb-0423 , Ho 607, ET 3.V.1632) and Joel (No. ffb-0424 , Ho 532, ET 7.IX.1628)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources / secondary literature ET 21.V. 1607 Dietz p. 104 and p. 270 Ho, Rabb S. Ho 410 HoNam p. 709: Grotwol Mich. (it should be called Sal.) HoEd Zl HoSt 755
2 CONT
2 CONT Website:  http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=ffb-0444
