1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 275	Hirsch bn David bn Juda haLevi seGal z”l, ish Horwitz 1604
2 CONT
2 CONT This man,  Hirsch bn David bn Juda haLevi seGal z”l, ish Horwitz 1604   is  buried with David, so obviously is his son, but his entry is written out in the Notes as “Hirsch Benjamin” followed by “Ari’ Hirsch bn David bn r’ Juda ha
2 CONC levi seGal”. The two unusual things being the mention of “Benjamin”, which I think was just a mistake by the person who wrote in non-Hebrew characters, and then the mention of “Ari” preceding Hirsch in the Hebrew portion. Nobody w
2 CONC ould make that up, and Ari’ is very rarely combined with Hirsch. So unless the person was reading from something which actually said “Zwi Hirsch” but was hard to decipher, causing him to read it as “Ari”, we need to be watching fo
2 CONC r this unusual name somewhere back in the Horwitz family or a maternal line. 
