1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Simon haLevi, ish Brandeis  1621/22
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Simon Brandeis HaLevi married in Prague, Gitele Loew, the Daughter of Maharal. They had one known son - Rabbi Samuel BRANDEIS.  According to one source? Died September 19, 1635 in Prague, Czechoslovakia - נפטר ז' תשרי ה'שצ"ו
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT The inscription on his tombstone (as per the museum records) states his death year 1622.
2 CONT
2 CONT As per Otto Muneles's כתובות מבית העלמין היהודי העתיק בפראג (Epitaphs from the ancient Jewish cemetery of Prague) in entry #206 for his wife Gitel, Shimon's death date is listed as Feb 22, 1622.  י"ב אדר ה'שפ"ב
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Simon BRANDEIS
2 CONT
2 CONT Gitele LOEW (d. 7 Tishre 1635) married Rabbi Simon BRANDEIS (d. 1635? Prague) in Prague of Levitic Origin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son was called Rabbi Samuel BRANDEIS (d. 1628 Prague).
2 CONT
2 CONT Gitele LOEW and Rabbi Simon BRANDEIS had a great-grandson called Israel BRANDEIS. Their great-grandson Israel BRANDEIS had two children: Roesel bat Israel BRANDEIS and Abraham Israel. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Brandeis is the name of a place near Prague, the capital of Bohemia. Here, in one of the oldest ghettos of Europe, members of the Brandeis family lived for generations.. ..In the ancient cemetery, among the 20,000 tombstones, coul
2 CONC d be found some with the name of Brandeis inscribed upon them-names of rabbis, merchants or artisans who belonged to Jewish guilds.." 
