1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi in Hungary, Ungarisch-Brod in Moravia (now [https://www.geni.com/projects/Jewish-Families-from-Uhersky-Brod-Ungarisch-Brod-Moravia-Czech-Republic/13157  Uherský Brod in the Czech Republic]) and [https://www.g
2 CONC eni.com/projects/Jewish-Families-from-Pozna%C5%84-Posen-Poland/16773 Posen ](1732-1736)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT After a serious illness he extended his name to Jakob Mordechai. Per David Kaufmann's research in 1897, this explains why on the first record on Sunday, August 4th 1709, in the parish register of Ung. Brod we see his signature as 
2 CONC Mordechai ha-Cohen, and he later always signs himself Jakob Mordechai ha-Cohen. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jakob Emden's own records of his time in the Moravian town of Ung. Brod provide the official register of the houses and inhabitants of the Jewish quarter of this town. There we see that in 1726, in the community house at No. 50, l
2 CONC ived Emden's father-in-law, Markus Naftali, with his wife Edl, his two unmarried sons Löbl and Herrsehl, an unmarried daughter Schöndl, the widowed cook Leye (Lea from Leipnik), and the maid Esther from Ung. Brod. Jakob Emden was 
2 CONC his son in law and married Jakob Mordechai's daughter Rachel in 1715. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT 1. Zu R. [https://www.jstor.org/stable/44757156 Jakob Emdens Selbstbiographie by David Kaufmann]
2 CONT Monatsschrift für Geschichte und Wissenschaft des Judentums, Jahrg. 41 (N. F. 5), H. 8 (1897), pp. 362-363 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Familie Wolf - by Ernst Wolf 1924, chart of family Latzko
2 CONT
