1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From M. Dworzhetsky, the History of Jewish Wladimir, in Pinkas Ludmir; sefer zikaron le-kehilat Ludmir:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Efraim Fishel ben Arieh Leib of Ludmir (1671 - 1719) (Rabbi Efraim the Lobbyist, Trustee of the House of Israel)
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Rabbi Tebel was a rabbi in Ludmir and a leader of the Council of the Four Lands (1717 - 1721).
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi David Tebel was also a resident of Ludmir and a financier of the Council of the Four Lands. He participated in a meeting of the abovementioned Council of 1721 and gave his Pinkas Vaad Arba Aratzot (rabbinic approbation) to t
2 CONC he work Damasek Eliezer (Jasienica Rosielna, 1723) by Rabbi Eliezer son of Jehuda, head of the rabbinic courtin Pinczow. In this Pinkas Vaad Arba Aratzot he is signed as: “David, that is, the insignificant Tebel of Ludmir, son of 
2 CONC the rabbi, the notable Rabbi Ephraim Fischel.”
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wunder, Elef Margoliot:
2 CONT
2 CONT The first son of Efraim Fishel ben Arieh Leib of Ludmir, he replaced his father as Treasurer of the Council of the Four Lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT     ***********************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Represented Volhinya region at Council of Four Lands: 1713, 1718 (1717, 1718), Table 6(i), p. 160: https://muse.jhu.edu/article/846614
