1 NOTE {geni:about_me} S.S.N.T.L. Naphtali Hirsch Katzenellenbogen (died after 1813) was the son of Eliezer (Lazarus) Katzenellenbogen of Bamberg and subsequently of Hagenau, 1755-1771.
2 CONT
2 CONT he was educated by his grandfather R' Samuel Helmann of Metz, and was rabbi (1794) at Frankfurt-on-the-Oder and then at Winzenheim, Alsace, and at the same time president of the consistory of the Upper Rhine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Naphtali Hirsch was one of the Rabbis at the Paris Sanhedrin, 1806, and had the reputation of being an excellent preacher.  He published "Sha'ar Naftali" (Frankfurt-on-the-Oder, 1797), a commentary to a part of Eben ha-'Ezer, toge
2 CONC ther with seventeen responsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the title page Naphtali Hirsch traces back his descent through nine generations. He left in manuscript "Sha'are Binah" a commentary to Hoshen Mishpat, and another commentary to Eben ha-'Ezer, as well as a volume of sermons and 
2 CONC ritual decisions, which are still in manuscript in the Strasbourg Library.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT Nepi-Ghirondi, Toledot Gedole Yisrael, pp 275 et seq,; R.E.J. xli. 125 [www.jewishencyclopaedia.com/articles/9238-katzenellenbogen]
