1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Schicks were descended from Rabbi Hanoch Heinich Schick of Shklov who is said to have married a daughter of. Rabbi Shlomo Zalman Rivlin.
2 CONT
2 CONT This Shlomo Zalman had a first cousin of the same name, who was the father of the Gaon of Vilna. Although various book sources give variant genealogies of Rabbi Hanochs' ancestry, there is no doubt that he was descended from two f
2 CONC amous scholars, Rabbi Yomtov Lipman Heller, the "Tosfot Yomtov" and Rabbi Meir Katzenellenbogen of Padua, the "Maharam Padua."
2 CONT
2 CONT In fact there are two explanations for the name Schick taken from each of the first letters of the words spelling "Shem Yisrael Kodesh" or "Shmuel Yuda Katzenellenbogen" - son of Rabbi Meir of Padua.
2 CONT
2 CONT R' Hanoch Heinich Schick, Av Beit Din Shklov was a contemporary of the Lubavitch Chassidic movement, R' Shneur Zalman of Liadi, author of Likutei Amarim ( or Baal HaTanya).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1804 edition of the tractate Avot with a commentary by the Gaon of Vilna, has an approbation by R' Hanoch.
2 CONT
2 CONT His eulogy was published in Evel Keramim, by Judah Leib, son of the ABD Orsha.
2 CONT
2 CONT For details on the Schick family see
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon Zvi Schick "MiMoshe Ad Moshe" (1903)
2 CONT
2 CONT David Tebele Efrati, "Toldot Anshei Shame (1875).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Torat Eidut HaZot, by Samuel Jungries, 1972.  "Tiferet Asher by Jacob Zvi Jungries 1976, "Imrei David (1964) by Jekutiel Mordecai Schick.
2 CONT
