1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/5622-eliezer-b-nathan-of-mayence '''Eliezer ben Nathan''']‬ (Hebrew: אליעזר בן נתן‬) of Mainz (1090–1170), or Ra'aven (ראב"ן‬), was a halakist and liturgical poet. As an earl
2 CONC y Rishon, he was a contemporary of the Rashbam and Rabbeinu Tam, and one of the earliest of the Tosafists. He was the son-in-law of Rabbi Eliakim b. Joseph of Mainz, a fellow student of Rashi. Through his four daughters Eliezer be
2 CONC came the ancestor of several learned families which exerted a great influence upon religious life in the subsequent centuries. One of his great-grandsons was R. Asher b. Jehiel (ROSH), father of R. Jacob, author of the Ṭurim.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%9C%D7%99%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8_%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A0%D7%AA%D7%9F
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.sefaria.org/person/Ra'avan
