1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HEILPRIN, JOEL BEN ISAAC:
2 CONT
2 CONT Polish Ḥasidic rabbi; lived at Ostrog in the middle of the seventeenth century. He was known as "Ba'al Shem I.," and, owing to his Talmudic and cabalistic learning, enjoyed a great reputation among his contemporaries, who called h
2 CONC im "a man of God." 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the cabalistic "Toledot Adam" (Zolkiev, 1720) it is recorded that in 1648 he miraculously saved some Jews who, pursued by enemies, had taken refuge in a ship. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of his writings were printed in the cabalistic "Mif'alot Elohim" (Zolkiev, 1724). See Ba'al Shem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography: Fuenn, Keneset Yisrael, pp. 432-43
2 CONT
2 CONT Read more: http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=529&letter=H#ixzz10sHqziEa
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT né en 1640?
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoel_Baal_Shem_(I)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From the JewishEncyclopedia.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joel b. Isaac Heilprin (Ba'al Shem I.) of Ostrog, Volhynia (1648-49)
2 CONT
2 CONT Polish Ḥasidic rabbi; lived at Ostrog in the middle of the seventeenth century.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was known as "Ba'al Shem I.," and, owing to his Talmudic and cabalistic learning, enjoyed a great reputation among his contemporaries, who called him "a man of God."
2 CONT
2 CONT In the cabalistic "Toledot Adam" (Zolkiev, 1720), it is recorded that in 1648 he miraculously saved some Jews who, pursued by enemies, had taken refuge in a ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of his writings were printed in the cabalistic "Mif'alot Elohim" (Zolkiev, 1724). See Ba'al Shem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography: Fuenn, Keneset Israel, pp. 432-43
2 CONT
2 CONT     *************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Represented Volhinya region at Council of Four Lands: 1689, 1691, 1691, 1700, 1713 (1699): Table 6(i), p. 159: https://muse.jhu.edu/article/846614
