1 NOTE {geni:about_me} אבד"ק ליסא ולונטשיץ
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Originally named Chaim. 'Yosef' added when he was ill. Rabbi in Lenczyca
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tidhar.tourolib.org/tidhar/view/3/1102
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Yosef Chaim Cara was Rabbi in Lissa (Leszno) and Lunshitz (Lenczyca), the great grandfather of the Zais Raanon. The information about the Zais Raanon given in http://www.tidhar.tourolib.org/tidhar/view/3/1102 The Zais Raanon
2 CONC  was the son-in-law of Zev Auerbach. Rabbi Yosef Chaim Cara's father was also named Yitzchak and was a rabbi in Hanover, Germany. He died in 1755. He is mentioned in the old Jewish Encyclopedia where his name is spelled "Isaac Sel
2 CONC ig Kara".
2 CONT
2 CONT Six generations after Rabbi Joseph Caro (the author of the Shulchan Aruch) a descendant of his was born who was named Rabbi Yosef Chaim Caro [the son of Rabbi Yitzchok Selig Kara of Hanover, Germany]. Rabbi Caro was known as the R
2 CONC av of Linschitz (Poland) and he served in this capacity for 80 years. He was a great man. He did not answer simple questions of Issur and Heter, but only the bigger questions, such as those involving a Din Torah. He knew how to an
2 CONC swer very quickly and no one would question the accuracy of his judgments. He was also very tall and people would tremble when he looked at them because of his greatness (Yirat Hakovoed). He died at 113 years of age. Rabbi Caro's 
2 CONC son-in-law was Rav Zeev Volf Ohrbach [Auerbach], who also became Rabbi of Linschitz, but only for a few years. When Rabbi Ohrbach died, his son-in-law, Rabbi Moshe Yehuda Leib ben Binyamin Beinish [known by the name of his book - 
2 CONC Zayit Raanan] took over as the Rabbi of Linschitz for one and one half years, after which he was called to serve [in succession in the towns of] Kovell, Lusk, [and] Dobreh, and finally in the town of Kutneh for many years. He then
2 CONC  went to Jerusalem and was head of all the Rabbis. He was the first Chief Rabbi of Jerusalem. His Bet Din consisted of Rabbi Shmuel Salant, the Rav of Kolish and himself. Nothing was done without him. These men were held in such e
2 CONC steem that the three pillars from the Churvah Synagogue (Rabbi Yehuda Hachasid's synagogue) two pillars from the table and one from the Aron Kodesh were used for the tombstones for those three rabbis. Zayit Raanan got the big one 
2 CONC from the Aron Kodesh. --------------------
