2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From Kaganoff, Benzion C. Jewish Surnames Through the Ages: An Etymological History. Commmentary, September 1, 1956:
2 CONT
2 CONT Zak comes from Zera K'doshim = "descendants of the martyrs."
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT From Geni.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adopted the surname Zak after the martyrdom of his brother Rabbi Mordechai Avdek Lublin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family name ZK - the initials of Zera Kadosh (seed of saints) - who gave their lives for Kiddush Hashem as stated in the book Shalshelet Zahav page 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ga'on Rabbi Meir Zak, Av Beit Din of Lvov, was a disciple of the Maharal of Lublin.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to family tradition, he is descended from the Baal Turim.
2 CONT
2 CONT See:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=48011&st=&pgnum=697&hilite=
2 CONT
