1 CONT G5.5. Benjamin Benas, married the daughter of R. Jacob Deltsch of Ludmir. Benjamin signed in the Pinkas (Minutes) of the Council of the Land of Lithuania a number of times between the years 1639 and 1655.
0 @N6000000003327798901@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.11. Esther, married R. Abraham Ashweig, son of MaHaRaSH, A.B.D. Brody.
0 @N6000000003327798908@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.12. Chaya, from the first marriage, married R. Leib b. Abraham Ettinge (Vienna, mentioned above, G5.8). She died at Zolkiew in 1632.  She was  also married to Mordecai, son of Abraham Shrentzel Rappoport, whose brother Simeon m
1 CONC arried her first cousin, Miriam (G4.12/5.4. below).
0 @N6000000003327798879@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.9. Beila, from the first wife (having the same name as the second wife  of Meir). She married R. Jonah son of Isaiah Teomim, A.B.D. of Grodno, and thereafter of Metz. He was the first member of the Teomim family to adopt the na
1 CONC me Teomim-Frankel. He was the author a Talmudic work Kikayon D'Yonah, published first in Amsterdam in 1699-70. A commentary by his son on the Torah appears in Leket Shmuel. He signed in the Pinkas (Minutes) of the Council  of the 
1 CONC Land of Lithuania in 1644, 1647, 1650 and 1655. He also wrote approbations to: 1.  Magid Meisharim by R. Joseph Caro, while he was in Grodno, published  in Lublin 1646. 2.  Yoreh Deah, also written in Grodno, published Cracow 1646
1 CONC . 3.  Choshen Mishpat, also written in Grodno, published Lublin 1654. 4.  Beit HaLevi by R. Isaiah HaLevi Horowitz, written in 1666 when he was A.B.D. of Metz of Posen, published Venice, 1666. He died on the first day of Passover 
1 CONC at Metz in 1669.
