1 CONT G6. Esther,  married R. Menachem Mendel Auerbach, A.B.D. Krotoschin,  author of Ateret Zekeinim (Chapter XII - Auerbach Family of Krotoschin).
0 @N6000000004398401329@ NOTE [Namiot2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT He was born in Cracow, where his father was rabbi of the community. On his father's death in 1671, Samuel Koidonover was appointed to succeed him, while Zechariah Mendel was appointed rabbi of the main synagogue. Some time after 1
1 CONC 674 he was appointed rabbi of Tvrobin and from 1691 to 1700, he was rabbi of Belz. Zechariah was an active member of the Council of Four Lands; his signature appears on takkanot of the council issued during the years 1688-1700.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the author of Ba'er Heitev on the Shulchan Aruch, Yoreh De'ah (in Sh. Ar. , Amsterdam, 1754) and Hoshen Mishpat (in Sh. Ar., ibid, 1762), a digest of the halachic comments on the Shulchan Aruch, similar to commentaries of t
1 CONC he same name by Judah b. Simeon Ashkenazi of Tiktin on Orah Hayyim, Yoreh De'ah, and Even ha-Ezer, by Isaiah b. Abraham on Orah Hayyim, and by Moses b. Simeon Frankfurter on Hoshen Mishpat. Later editions of the Shulchan Aruch gen
1 CONC erally contain Zechariah Mendel's Ba'er Heitev to Yoreh De'ah and Hoshen Mishpat and that of Ashkenazi to Orah Hayyim and Even ha-Ezer.
1 CONT Encyclopaedia Judaica, Vol. 16 p. 959
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the Av bet din of Belz according to the reference in the Shulchan Aruch.
