0 @N6000000001234952116@ NOTE Grand Rabbi of Metz 1750-1764 (S: Meyer: TAbles du registre d'etat civil... Metz  1717-1972)
1 CONT
1 CONT S:Otsar Harabanim (19126) 
1 CONT      5453 (1693) among the leaders of the Council of the 4 lands in Yaroslav
1 CONT      5488 (1728) Rabbi in Mannheim, Muenster
1 CONT      5520 (1760) Rabbi in Metz
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources for the tree: 
1 CONT      * Da'at Qedoshim (by Shmuel Wiener: St. Petersburg, Russia; 1897¬98) Contains information about the ancestors, children, and grandchildren of Rabbi Shmuel Hillman of Metz (1670¬1764).
1 CONT
1 CONT      * Tables du registre d')tat civil de la communaut) juive de
1 CONT Metz ¬ 1717¬1792, (by Pierre¬Andr) Meyer: Paris, France; 1987)  Contains detailed birth/death/marriage information about Rabbi Shmuel Hillman, his wife, children, and grandchildren.
1 CONT
1 CONT      * Ohalei Shem (p.450, by Shmuel Noah Gotleib: Pinsk, Russia;
1 CONT 1912) Contains a biography of Rabbi Shmuel Yitzhak Hillman and his ancestors, including the fact that he was a direct descendant of the above¬mentioned Rabbi Shmuel Hillman of Metz. 
1 CONT
1 CONT      * Entseqlopedia le¬Khalutsei ha¬Yishuv u¬Vonav ,  (Vol. IV,
1 CONT p.1796, by David Tidhar: Tel Aviv, Israel) Contains additional biographical information about Rabbi Shmuel Yitzhak Hillman and his ancestors, including the fact that he was a direct descendant of the above¬mentioned Rabbi Shmuel H
1 CONC illman of Metz.  The author of this source and that of Ohalei Shem give different dates of birth for Rabbi Shmuel
1 CONT Yitzhak Hillman.
1 CONT
1 CONT      * Note on our ancestry through the children and grandchildren of Rabbi Shmuel Hillman of Metz. This Rabbi had four children, two which were sons. One son Moshe had a daughter who married and thus did not retain the family nam
1 CONC e Hillman. (See Da'at Qedoshim, p. 65).  The other son ¬ Uri Faivush  had two sons: Shlomo (Salomon) Leib and Juziel (See Tables du registre d'etat civil...).  Since the names Shlomo and Leib then occur in later generations of bot
1 CONC h our family and Rebetzen Sarah Hillman Herzog's family, and the name Juziel does not, I believe we ar
1 CONT descended from Shlomo Leib.
1 CONT
1 CONT      * Since Rabbi Shmuel Hillman of Metz died in 1764, we can be
1 CONT almost 100% assured that his descendants named children
1 CONT thereafter for him. Hence I postulate that Shlomo Leib Hillman
1 CONT had a son named Shmuel was could not have been born until
1 CONT ca.1780, given that this Shmuel's father Shlomo Leib was born in
1 CONT 1757 (See Tables du registre d'etat civil.
1 CONT
