1 CONT almost 100% assured that his descendants named children
1 CONT thereafter for him. Hence I postulate that Shlomo Leib Hillman
1 CONT had a son named Shmuel was could not have been born until
1 CONT ca.1780, given that this Shmuel's father Shlomo Leib was born in
1 CONT 1757 (See Tables du registre d'etat civil.
0 @N6000000009752722574@ NOTE Rabbi
0 @N6000000009752722582@ NOTE Rabbi
0 @N6000000009752722610@ NOTE Grand rabbin de France en 1363
0 @N6000000004588074925@ NOTE []
1 CONT
1 CONT According to the Jewish Encyclopedia (Vol. 11, p.523, #23), he was the son of Samson Spira, rabbi at Grodno, and died in 1577.  Wrote under the title "Imrei Shefer" - commentaries on Rashi and Eliah Mizrachi - published by his son
1 CONC      saac in Lublin in 1586/1597
0 @N6000000003327798830@ NOTE
1 CONT G2.2. Bonah, married R. Jacob, son of R. Moses HaLevi.
0 @N6000000003327792249@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.4. R. Jacob Katzenellenpogen,6 succeeded his father as A.B.D. of Lvov  and was also the Head of the Yeshiva. He died there on February 28th  (13th Adar), 1660. His name appeared a few times in the Records of the  Council of the
1 CONC  Four Lands. He is men
0 @N6000000003327789314@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.1. Wife of R. Moses Isaac, Dayan of Cracow (died there in 1650), son  of R. Jacob Reinbac3
0 @N6000000003327792168@ NOTE
1 CONT G5.3. Eidel, married R. Jacob Isaac Chajes, Judge and Moreh Zedek  (Teacher) of Prague, where he died in 1687, son of R. Eliezer Chajes of  Cracow, died in 1623.5
0 @N6000000003327798345@ NOTE
1 CONT G4.13. Ogla, married R. Hirsch, son of Abraham Alpersch of Posen.  Fifth Generation
